symbol collect
lines 0 91
hash 27681f4712bb05f4
note The walk that produces symbols. Named children of the root become symbols; imports go to ImportText::record; comments, package clauses, attributes and bodyless 'mod foo;' are skipped. Containers (impl, mod, trait, class) recurse exactly one level so methods appear with their owner type, which is what gives depth 1 symbols and what a qualified call later binds against; a container itself has no calls. A symbol's name is the grammar's name field, else impl_name for a Rust impl, else its first line up to a brace or '::' (Odin's foo :: proc), dropped past 80 characters because a bad guess is a whole line of code; Odin attributes such as @(test) are part of the declaration node, so that guess reads the line after them. A bodyless 'mod foo;' is a reference, and as a symbol it would pull every .map() call to 'mod map;'. A container's owner is its type field (Rust impl X for Y gives Y) or, for a class, its own name. A node ending at column 0 of a line ends on the line before.

