file crates/index/src/parse.rs
symbol record
lines 0 80
hash 0661663d60d2426e
note Every import statement in the file, reduced to a map of name-or-alias to module stem. Deliberately string work rather than per-language parsing: it only has to be good enough for resolve to send an unqualified or aliased call to the right file. Two shapes: a quoted module (Odin import "core:fmt" or import alias "../pkg", JS import {a, b} from './mod') maps every identifier before the quote to the module's last path segment, or the module to itself when none is named; anything else is a path plus items (Rust use a::b::{c, d as e}, Python from a.b import c, d or import a.b), and each item or its alias maps to the last segment of the path.

